# auth-sso — empty env templates (mirrors the `env:` list in module.manifest).
# The generator appends these (blank) to the project's .env.example section; set
# real values in .env and NEVER commit them.
#
# WHAT YOU MUST SET to turn SSO on for a project:
#   1. OIDC_ISSUER_URL  — the Keycloak realm URL (see SETUP.md). One realm can
#                         serve many projects, so this is usually the SAME value
#                         across your projects, e.g.:
#                           https://auth.example.com/realms/pi
#                         Left blank, auth is OFF: the frontend login routes return
#                         503 and the backend's protected endpoint returns 503 —
#                         the rest of the app keeps working (graceful fallback).
#   2. The per-project CLIENT credentials — these reuse the slots the base ALREADY
#      added to this project's .env.example section (do NOT add new ones here):
#           <PREFIX>_OIDC_CLIENT_ID       (e.g. CLINIC_OIDC_CLIENT_ID)
#           <PREFIX>_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET   (e.g. CLINIC_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET)
#      Create a confidential client per project in the realm (SETUP.md) and paste
#      its id + secret there. The frontend session is encrypted with the base's
#      <PREFIX>_APP_SECRET (also already in the section) — set that too.
#
OIDC_ISSUER_URL=
#
# OPTIONAL — the backend's expected token audience ("aud"). Leave blank to accept
# the project's own client id as the audience (the common Keycloak setup once you
# add an audience mapper — see SETUP.md). Set it only to require a different value.
OIDC_AUDIENCE=
#
# OPTIONAL overrides — leave BLANK and the compose fragment derives the correct
# public URLs from the project's subdomain + ${BASE_DOMAIN}:
#   redirect    -> https://<subdomain>.${BASE_DOMAIN}/api/auth/callback
#   post-logout -> https://<subdomain>.${BASE_DOMAIN}/
# Set them only if your project is reached at a non-derived URL. The redirect URI
# you register in the Keycloak client MUST match this exactly (SETUP.md).
OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=
OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend-only knobs (NOT in the env: contract list — the compose fragment passes
# them with safe defaults; override in .env only if you need to):
#   OIDC_REQUIRE_HTTPS_METADATA=false  Allow the backend/frontend to fetch the
#                         realm metadata over HTTP or an untrusted (local CA) TLS
#                         cert. Defaults to true (production). Set false ONLY for
#                         local *.localhost testing against Caddy's internal CA.
#   OIDC_SCOPE="openid profile email"  Scopes the frontend requests at login.
#   OIDC_APP_BASE_URL                  The app's public base URL (derived from the
#                         subdomain by default); used to build absolute redirects.
